.TH MINICODE 1 "November 2026" "minicode" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
minicode \- small editor for text, code, and LaTeX, with a browser and terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B minicode
.RB [ \-\-foreground ]
.RI [ path ]
.br
.B minicode
.BR \-v " | " \-\-version
.br
.B minicode
.BR \-h " | " \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B minicode
opens a window with a file tree on the left and an editor on the right.
.PP
If
.I path
is a folder, it becomes the root of the file tree. If it is a file, the
file is opened and the tree is rooted at the folder that holds it. With no
argument the current directory is opened.
.PP
minicode runs as a single instance. Running it again while it is open
passes the path to the running instance, which opens a new window on that
folder, or brings forward the window that already has it and shows the file
there, and the command returns at once.
.PP
Started from a terminal, the command returns as soon as the window is up,
and minicode runs apart from the terminal, as VS Code's
.B code
does: closing the terminal leaves minicode open, and the terminal gives no
warning about a running process. What minicode prints after that goes
nowhere, unless it was sent to a file. A problem before the window, such as
no display to open it on, is printed in the terminal, and the command exits
with minicode's status.
.PP
Ctrl+Shift+H shows every keyboard shortcut in the window.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-foreground
Stay in the terminal until minicode quits, as any program run there does,
with its output in the terminal. Closing the terminal then closes minicode.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a summary of the usage and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-
End the options; what follows is a path, even when it starts with a dash.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/minicode/settings.conf
Colors, opacity, and language server commands. Ctrl+, creates it with every
setting commented out and opens it. It follows
.BR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME .
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/minicode/bin/tectonic
Where the LaTeX preview puts tectonic when it is asked to download it.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MINICODE_FOREGROUND
Set to anything but an empty value or 0, the same as
.BR \-\-foreground ,
for scripts and debugging.
.TP
.B MINICODE_SETTINGS
A settings file to read in place of the one above.
.TP
.B MINICODE_TECTONIC
The tectonic binary the LaTeX preview uses, ahead of any other.
.TP
.B MINICODE_LSP_LOG
A file to append every language server message to, for debugging.
.TP
.B SHELL
The shell the terminal panel runs.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1),
.BR clangd (1)
.PP
